      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T19:38:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These limits have different consequences from their skcms equivalents. skcms borrows table and CLUT data, while this rust parser copies it into `Vec`s. For example, the 350M-point limit can permit a CLUT copy larger than 1 GiB, and a 16M-entry gray curve is copied into each of the three TRCs. Should we impose a profile-size or total-owned-data limit appropriate for codec input before making these allocations?",
      "revId": "8650246985d8ec27eeb64b90415ad6ca4980a4ab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa4b9747_e168d01c",
        "filename": "rust/icc/FFI.rs",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 144,
      "author": {
        "id": 6035
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-28T17:48:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Very good point. I added the `IccReader` class, which has a `read_vec` function, which will:\n- first, get the slice for the appropriate number of bytes\n  - this means that if we read past the end of the buffer, we fail here\n- then, allocate and pad (for SIMD) the buffer, and copy the data in\n\nThat way, we\u0027ll never allocate more than the tag-size in one of these vectors. The worst case scenario is where we reference the same offset multiple times and re-allocate the buffer because of that.",
      "parentUuid": "041286f5_a34453a5",
      "revId": "8650246985d8ec27eeb64b90415ad6ca4980a4ab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d56882e_55b2b043",
        "filename": "rust/icc/FFI.rs",
        "patchSetId": 8
