      "writtenOn": "2026-08-27T22:11:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if there is a way to avoid these repetitive `let foo \u003d match ... return false` blocks somehow.\n\nOne way to do this may be to change the return type to `Option\u003c()\u003e` - then `?` works in `let version \u003d match read_u32(\u0026header[8..12])?;`.  (An outer, C/C++/FFI-friendly function can then translate `Some(())` to `true` and `None` to false - just `ret_val.is_some()`.)\n\nA slightly less disruptive (but not sure if as effective) way may be to use `let ... else` - e.g.:\n\n```\n    let Some(version) \u003d read_u32(\u0026header[8..12]) else { return false; };\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 882,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 885,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "8650246985d8ec27eeb64b90415ad6ca4980a4ab",
